r DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus ('owned by ... a political subdivision', 'used for the transportation of persons for compensation'), and whether ru.transit_bus is excluded or covered under DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus. The record is otherwise faithful. The coder's rule and witnesses (forbid, permit, idle, blind, branch_1, branch_2) are expected to pass once these classes are decided.\", \"nearest\": [\"ru.aggregate: 'true when the user carries an included class, unknown when no included class holds and the user carries an unresolved class' — with no included class under DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus, membership is never true\", \"ru.bus: 'motor vehicle designed to carry many passengers' — says nothing of the definition's more-than-10 design capacity, its owners (State, political subdivision, private school or nursery) or use for compensation, and the ru.aggregate contract excludes it as a stand-in for an admitted aggregate\", \"ru.transit_bus: 'bus in public transit service, identifiable by its livery or route display' — the run's reading leaves it unresolved under both DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus and DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus\", \"ru.tour_bus_or_limousine: 'a tour or shuttle bus, or a lengthened passenger vehicle for hire' — it includes limousines, which DEF-LVMC-11-02-150 leaves out ('other than a limousine')\", \"ru.occupant_count: 'the number of persons in or on a vehicle' — a count of persons present, not the number of passengers the vehicle is designed to carry\"]}}\n"}}}
